          "new_text": "def matrix_free_spectral_embedding(\n    counts: np.ndarray,\n    n_components: int,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return leading spectral coordinates for a cell-by-feature count matrix.\"\"\"\n\n    if not isinstance(counts, np.ndarray) or counts.ndim != 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"counts must be a 2D numpy array\")\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(counts)):\n        raise ValueError(\"counts contains nonfinite values\")\n    if np.any(counts < 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"counts contains negative values\")\n    if np.any(np.array(counts.sum(axis=1)).flatten() == 0):\n        raise ValueError(\"counts has all-zero cell rows\")\n    n_cells, n_features = counts.shape\n    if not (1 <= n_components < n_cells):\n        raise ValueError(\"n_components must be in [1, n_cells-1]\")\n\n    # IDF scaling\n    df = np.array((counts > 0).sum(axis=0)).flatten().astype(float)\n    idf = np.log(n_cells / (1.0 + df))\n    X = counts * idf[np.newaxis, :]\n\n    # Row normalization\n    norms = np.linalg.norm(X, axis=1)\n    X = X / norms[:, np.newaxis]\n\n    # Linear operator for X X^T\n    def matvec(v):\n        return X @ (X.T @ v)\n\n    A = LinearOperator((n_cells, n_cells), matvec=matvec, dtype=X.dtype)\n\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(random_state)\n    v0 = rng.randn(n_cells).astype(X.dtype)\n    eigenvalues, eigenvectors = eigsh(A, k=n_components, which=\"LA\", v0=v0)\n\n    # Convert to eigenvalues of W = X X^T - I and sort descending\n    eigenvalues_w = eigenvalues - 1.0\n    eigenvalues_desc = eigenvalues_w[::-1]\n    eigenvectors_desc = eigenvectors[:, ::-1]\n\n    return eigenvalues_desc, eigenvectors_desc"
